{
  "_note": [
    "Step 07 PR 07b — C1 Checkpoint-0 selection replay CORPUS (hand-authored).",
    "Design: docs/design/generic_framework_upgrade/step_07_tuner_policy_and_training_diagnostics/pr_07b_tuner_policy.md §5 / C1.",
    "Each history names ONE awkward case the selection/threshold helpers must keep",
    "handling identically after the MetricOrder rewire (C2) and the scale-rule",
    "classification (C3). Non-finite scores travel as the sentinel STRINGS",
    "'__neg_inf__' / '__pos_inf__' / '__nan__' (decoded by the test) so the fixture",
    "stays strict-JSON parseable — the same reason _json_safe_reference refuses to",
    "persist bare Infinity/NaN.",
    "Record shape: only the fields the audited helpers actually read —",
    "status, denoising_score, is_trial, memory.time_mode, health_gate_enabled",
    "(the DS5 self-describing waiver that makes a successful finite record VALID),",
    "health_gate_results (for the UNKNOWN/INVALID validity cases).",
    "2026-08-16 Step 07 correction: 'h_time_mode_mismatch' became",
    "'h_time_metadata_not_role'. The old case asserted a two-field agreement",
    "rule (is_trial AND memory.time_mode) that production could never violate",
    "— both derive from the same plan.is_trial — and whose real effect was to",
    "discard every valid trial in a run launched without time budgets. The",
    "replacement carries that reachable no-budget shape instead."
  ],
